{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552808-media-about-the-arcana","id":1552808,"title":"Media about the Arcana","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-01T11:16:31-07:00","id":1552808,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Media about the Arcana","content":"<br /> I made a list of movies (and a few TV series, video games, novels, etc) that embody each Arcanum or give examples of what their use might look like; the characters aren't necessarily mages, but each one is about people encountering some manifestation(s) of one or more Arcana. If a new player doesn't &quot;get&quot; a given Arcanum, my hope is that STs can point them towards this list for inspiration and guidance (and maybe get a few ideas themselves). Some entries could be filed under more than one Arcanum (Death and Spirit in particular), and I've tried to avoid overlap and duplication wherever possible.<br /> <br /> Let me know how I got them wrong.<ul><li><b>Death</b>: 13 Ghosts, Beetlejuice, Bleach, Death Becomes Her, Fatal Frame, Final Destination, Ghostbusters, Ghost Reaper Girl, The Halloween Tree, In Time (2011),The Masque of the Red Death, Meet Joe Black, Old, Pushing Daisies, ReAnimator, The Sixth Sense, The Woman in Black</li> <li><b>Fate</b>: The Bottle Imp, The Butterfly Effect, Donnie Darko, It Could Happen To You, Oedipus Rex, Only You, Sliding Doors, The Time Traveler's Wife</li> <li><b>Forces</b>: Backdraft, Chernobyl, Equilibrium (2002), Gravity, The Matrix, Oppenheimer, The Perfect Storm, A Quiet Place, Radioactive, Wanted</li> <li><b>Life</b>: 28 Days Later, Avatar (2009), Come into My Cellar, Frankenstein; or, The Modern Prometheus, Gattaca, The Girl with All the Gifts, The Island of Dr Moreau, Jurassic Park/Jurassic World, Little Shop of Horrors, Logan, Nausica\u00e4 of the Valley of the Wind, Outbreak (1995), Princess Mononoke, The Stand, Unbreakable, Yuuzhan Vong biotechnology (Star Wars EU)</li> <li><b>Matter</b>: Avatar: The Last Airbender, Backdraft, Big Hero 6, Breaking Bad, The Cave of Forgotten Dreams, Daredevil: Born Again, Fullmetal Alchemist, Mythbusters, October Sky, &quot;A Piece of Wood&quot;, <i>The Wheel of Time</i>'s magic system (a.k.a. &quot;weaving&quot;), The Wind Rises</li> <li><b>Mind</b>: The Animatrix, The Boy and the Heron, Dark City, The Dream Cycle of H.P. Lovecraft, Eternal Darkness: Sanity's Requiem, Eternal Sunshine of the Spotless Mind, The Fisher King, Ghost in the Shell (1995), The Haunting (1963), Inception, The Lathe of Heaven, Memento, A Midsummer Night\u2019s Dream, A Nightmare on Elm Street, Pan's Labyrinth, Paprika, Pi, Psychonauts, The Sandman, Village of the Damned (1960)</li> <li><b>Prime</b>: The Books of Magic, Doctor Strange, The Great Encyclopedia Of Faeries by Pierre Dubois, Harry Potter, Howl's Moving Castle, Jonathan Strange &amp; Mr Norrell, Merlin (1998), Promethea, The Sorcerer's Apprentice, The Spiderwick Chronicles, The Tempest</li> <li><b>Space</b>: 2001: A Space Odyssey, Cosmos: A Personal Voyage, Everything Everywhere All At Once, House of Leaves, The Hyperion Cantos, Jumper, Portal, The Prestige</li> <li><b>Spirit</b>: The Exorcist, Ghostbusters, Heart and Souls, The Legend of Zelda: Twilight Princess, Merkabah Rider: High Planes Drifter, Spirited Away, What Dreams May Come</li> <li><b>Time</b>: Arrival (a.k.a. &quot;The Story of Your Life\u201d by Ted Chiang), Back to the Future Trilogy, Braid, Chrono Trigger, Clockstoppers, The Curious Case of Benjamin Button, Doctor Who, The Flash (2014 TV series), Groundhog Day, Interstellar, The Legend of Zelda: Majora's Mask, The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time, Looper, &quot;Night Meeting&quot; (<i>The Martian Chronicles</i>), Prince of Persia: The Sands of Time, Run Lola Run, Slaughterhouse-Five, A Sound of Thunder, The Terminator, The Time Traveler's Wife</li> </ul>(And if course there's <i>Dune</i>, which covers just about all of the Arcana at one point or another...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":6327,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","user":"Super_Dave","date":". 01-26-2026, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-31T01:00:44-07:00","id":1554888,"title":"","content":"Don\u2019t forget the Beetlejuice Beetlejuice movie that came out last year!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-20T18:05:46-08:00","id":1556868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552808-media-about-the-arcana?p=1554888#post1554888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t forget the Beetlejuice Beetlejuice movie that came out last year!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I've seen it, thought it was alright. I assumed that whenever a franchise was mentioned, people would intuit that the recommendation extends to the other entries in that series as well. I mean, within reason: some sequels are crap and everyone knows it, so a recommendation for a given property doesn't necessarily extend to everything in its franchise, but for the most part if the original was relevant then the sequels are likely to explore similar themes and ideas, and so are worth at least looking into.<br /> <br /> P.S. I've alphabetized the list and added a few new titles as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/